==Norwegian Nynorsk==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|nn|/doː/}} {{nn-pronu-note}}
* In the third sense of the adverb, it should always be pronounced unstressed.

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|nn|non|þá}}, from {{inh|nn|gem-pro|*þan||then}}. Its use as a conjunction can be seen as taken from the {{der|nn|non|-}} combination {{m|non|þá er}} ({{m|non|er}} being the actual conjunction).

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|nn|da}}
* {{l|nn|daa}} {{q|obsolete spelling}}

====Conjunction====
{{head|nn|conjunction}}

# [[when]] (at a time in the past)
#: {{ux|nn|'''Då''' morgonen kom, hadde vêret vorte betre.|'''When''' the morning came, the weather had gotten better.}}
# [[since]], [[as]] {{q|used to denote a reason}}
#: {{syn|nn|ettersom}}

====Adverb====
{{head|nn|adverb}}

# [[then]] {{gloss|at that time}}
#: {{ux|nn|Fyrst '''då''' kan me gjera noko med det.|We can't do anything about it until '''then'''.}}
# [[then]] (in that case)
#: {{usex|nn|'''Då''' er eg redd det er lite me kan gjera.|'''Then''' I am afraid there is little we can do.}}
# [[yet]], [[still]], [[though]]

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|nn|dåtid}}
* {{l|nn|no og då}}

===Etymology 2===
{{wikipedia|lang=nn|Dåslekta}}
[[File:Galeopsis tetrahit - kare kõrvik Keilas.jpg|thumb|[[kvassdå|kvass'''då''']], the common hemp-nettle]]
From {{der|nn|non|ákrdái}}, whence also {{cog|sv|dån}}. Related to {{m|nn|døy||to die}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|nn|dæ|g=m|g2=f}}, {{l|nn|dæe|g=m}}

====Noun====
{{nn-noun-m1}}

# {{senseid|nn|hemp-nettle}} a [[hemp-nettle]]

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|nn|dundå}}
* {{l|nn|guldå}}
* {{l|nn|kvassdå}}
* {{l|nn|smaldå}}
* {{l|nn|vrangdå}}

===References===
* {{R:The Nynorsk Dictionary}}

